course: dictionary
lesson: 8024
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name something your body does for you, without you deciding to do it. «Closing your eyes when you sneeze is a reflex.» A reflex is quick and automatic, so you do not stop to think about it first.
explain: The word can also describe how fast you react. «The goalkeeper has fast reflexes.» Here reflexes means how quickly she can move when the ball is coming at her. Reflexes is the plural form, and it is a noun.
explain: In maths, reflex is a different meaning. A reflex angle is bigger than 180 degrees but smaller than 360 degrees. The same word can mean something new in a new subject, so look at the clues around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: A reflex is something your body does quickly, without deciding to.
fact: A reflex action is one you do automatically, such as blinking when something flies at your eye.
fact: Reflexes means how quickly you can react, as with a goalkeeper with fast reflexes.
fact: In maths, a reflex angle is between 180 and 360 degrees.
fact: «A reflex is a quick automatic movement»: in the knee-jerk test, the doctor taps your knee and the signal goes to the spinal cord and straight back to the muscle.
exercise: «Closing your eyes when you sneeze is a reflex.» What is a reflex here? | A slow, careful movement | A loud kind of sneeze | *Something your body does quickly without deciding to | A thing you decide to do after thinking very hard
exercise: «The goalkeeper has fast reflexes.» What does reflexes mean here? | The number of goals you have saved | *How quickly you can react | How tired you feel | The size of your gloves
exercise: In maths, what is a reflex angle? | An angle of exactly 90 degrees | An angle smaller than 90 degrees | *An angle bigger than 180 degrees but smaller than 360 degrees | A line that goes straight across
test: «A reflex is a quick automatic movement.» What does automatic mean here? | *Done without deciding | Done with a loud noise | Done only with a grown-up's help | Done very slowly after a long think
test: Which angle is a reflex angle? | *240 degrees | 180 degrees | 45 degrees | 90 degrees
exam: Which of these is a reflex action? | Choosing a book from the shelf | Writing a story in your best handwriting | *Blinking when something flies at your eye | Reading the menu before you order
